# Fix OnlyOffice [object Object] Error

The user is seeing an `Errore OnlyOffice: [object Object]` error when trying to open the editor in Proposal or Content Library sections. This is due to the frontend not stringifying the error object received from OnlyOffice, and likely caused by a JWT secret mismatch between the backend and OnlyOffice services.

## Proposed Changes

### Frontend

#### [MODIFY] [OnlyOfficeEditor.tsx](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/frontend/src/pages/OnlyOfficeEditor.tsx)
- Update the [onError](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/frontend/src/pages/OnlyOfficeEditor.tsx#152-160) handler to stringify the `event` object, allowing the user to see the actual error code and description.

### Infrastructure

#### [MODIFY] [docker-compose.yml](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/docker-compose.yml)
- Pass `ONLYOFFICE_JWT_SECRET` to the `backend` service environment to ensure it remains consistent with the [onlyoffice](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/backend/app/api/onlyoffice.py#366-499) service when set via environment variables.

#### [MODIFY] [.env.example](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/.env.example)
- Add `ONLYOFFICE_JWT_SECRET` to the example file to guide the user on setting it correctly.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. **Frontend Detail Check**: After applying the frontend change, ask the user to refresh the page. Instead of `[object Object]`, they should see something like `Errore OnlyOffice: {"error": -7, "description": "..."}` or similar. This will confirm the exact cause (e.g., code -7 is JWT error).
2. **JWT Secret Test**: If the error was indeed a JWT mismatch, applying the [docker-compose.yml](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/docker-compose.yml) change and restarting with `docker compose up -d` should resolve the issue. If the user hasn't set a secret, both will fallback to the same default and it should also work.
3. **Connectivity Check**: Verify if the OnlyOffice container can reach `tw-backend:8000`. If the error persists with a network-related code (e.g., -4), further investigation into Docker networking may be needed.
